  "notes": "Piano-driven power-ballad pop with a falsetto ceiling. ⚠ `confidence` is low, and the research is the reason: it rates the entry medium-low and says outright that \"instruments and genre are documented; the register/tempo/harmony detail is inferred from the lane and marked accordingly\". Everything below the instrument list is therefore a reading, and only three claims here are researched facts. First, the terracing: \"verses drumless or kick-only; chorus enters with a big reverbed backbeat, layered claps and tom cascades\", which is `kick.densityPerBar` 0—4 with `fourOnFloorInChorus`, a large-reverb snare under a doubled clap stack, `tom` fills and the snare-roll ladder off. Second, the tracking: \"he plays drums, guitar and piano on his own recordings, so the kit feel is played rather than gridded\", which is a loose humanize block rather than a quantised one. Third, the low end: \"no 808. Sustained synth or electric bass on roots doubling the kick; sub swell as the chorus trigger\", so no `bass808` block is authored and the bassline is a near-static kick mirror. Harmony is \"piano and keyboards as the primary chordal instruments with close triads and a pedal-tone left hand; 4-bar loops\" with \"a plagal chorus cadence\", so the IV—I family leads and `voicing.style` is close with a high `triad` share. Melody encodes \"ascend by 3rds through the verse and pre-chorus and resolve on a sustained high note\" as a third-weighted interval spread over an arch contour with the highest `octaveJumpProb` in this batch for the documented falsetto leap; \"harmony is octave-doubled rather than in thirds\" is the `octave_echo` counter. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are every drum probability, the humanize numbers, the melody register, the harmonic weights and `bpm.mode` 100 (the midpoint of the stated 90—110 ballad core), and the entry's own [LOW-CONF] mark on the tenor-ceiling claim is repeated here.",
